# Files that are executed on the Linux host MUST keep LF endings. Checked out
# with CRLF on Windows and copied to the server, a shell script fails with
# "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M" and a systemd unit silently misparses.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
Caddyfile       text eol=lf
deploy/**       text eol=lf

# Keep SQL migrations byte-stable so Drizzle's migration hashes don't shift
# between a Windows and a Linux checkout.
*.sql           text eol=lf
drizzle/**      text eol=lf
